# Act 1: Cast On. The format is described at the top of scripts/story.gd.
# Flow (Alex's design, 2026-11-12; every line here is a draft for Alex):
# act1_arrival: a new game opens on the rain bus. She walks to the Welcome to Maple Grove sign, the
#   rain stops, the arrival music swells, the camera takes in the town (Giorgio at his stall, Barbara
#   on her round) and comes back to her face. Wren the mayor (brisk, busy, stressed) welcomes her and
#   points out each shop from the sign, then leaves her free (Alex, 2026-11-14: the player explores
#   as they like; the only goal is Gran's house). The shopkeepers say hello when she first talks to
#   them (meet_<id> below), and short control hints come up as she goes (main.gd _update_hints).
# The cast is Alex's of 2026-11-12: Rosa has the Yarn Barn and the market stall, Gary Willow Homes,
#   Giorgio Heart Bakery, Steve Builder's Delight, Sabrina the Coffee Shop, Barbara the post.
# act1_note (inside): Gran's note on the coffee table (she's gone to Florida and Nora minds the farm;
#   Alex, 2026-11-13: Gran is alive), kept in her bag; 100 coins; rent to Gran's tin.
# The guided opening (Alex, 2026-11-16, docs/DIRECTION.md): Gran leaves her yarn and needles, not
#   coins → knit in the rocking chair → act1_knit (memory thread #1, then a knock: Wren, who wants
#   to buy it; the haggle panel opens in its guided form, scripts/sweater_sale.gd open_guided) →
#   act1_sold ("first_sale": Wren sends her to Steve for seed and Rosa for yarn) → act1_seeds
#   ("seeds_bought") → act1_planted ("planted") → act1_yarn ("yarn_bought") → knit again →
#   act1_knit2 → act1_market (Rosa buys the second; bleating from the farm) → act1_strays (meet
#   Rowan; "you'll want a pen") → act1_wood (the pen builder, F, and gate crafting, G) → act1_pen
#   ("pen_built") → herd them in, on foot or playing the dog → act1_flock ("sheep_penned") →
#   act1_porch (the voicemail, Rowan's lantern) → end card. After that she isn't guided any more.

== act1_arrival
@trigger start
@once
@weather rain
@home rowan 25.6 -5.5
@place nora 31.6 3.3 90
@prop bus bus 33.8 0.6 0
@prop suitcase case 32.2 3.6 20
@place giorgio 58.5 -5.2 -45
@place barbara 42.36 -7.6 180
@face barbara 42.36 -9.0
@place wren 44.6 2.2 270
@fade out 0.01
@title Knitting Empire
@camera 32.6 2.2 10
@fade in 2.0
> Last stop. The rain has followed her all the way from the city.
@prop_move bus 72 0.6 6
> The bus pulls away and takes the last of the engine noise with it. One suitcase. A coat that was never meant for weather like this.
Nora (worried): Okay. Nobody followed. Nobody knows you're here.
@phone Unknown number
> Her phone buzzes. No name. It doesn't need one.
@camera nora 5
? The phone keeps ringing.
- Decline the call. -> declined | phone off; set declined_max
- Let it ring out. -> ringout | phone off; set ignored_max
@label declined
> She presses the red button, then holds the side button until the screen goes black. Her hand is shaking.
Nora (neutral): Not today. Not here.
@goto after
@label ringout
> She watches it ring until it stops. Then a little longer, in case.
Nora (sad): It'll stop. It has to stop eventually.
@label after
@prop_remove bus
> She hauls the suitcase up by its one good handle. Through the rain, up ahead, a painted sign.
@prop_remove case
# the sign beat follows the sign wherever the world editor puts it
@walk nora by welcome_sign -1.4 3.6
@face nora by welcome_sign 0 0
@camera by welcome_sign 0 0.6 6
@wait 1.2
> WELCOME TO MAPLE GROVE. Someone keeps the paint fresh.
@weather clear
@music arrival
> And as she reads it, the rain stops. Just like that, like somebody turned off a tap.
@camera 50 -2 19
@wait 2.5
> Woodsmoke. Wet cobbles drying in the sun. Somewhere, bread.
@camera giorgio 7 yaw -45
@wait 1.0
> Giorgio the baker is selling the morning's loaves from his stall, still warm enough to steam.
@camera barbara 7
@wait 1.0
> Barbara the postwoman is on her round: a letter for every door, and a kind word for everyone who opens one.
@face nora by welcome_sign 0.8 5.8
@camera nora 3 low yaw 45
@wait 1.0
Nora (warm): I think I'm going to like it here.
@walk wren by welcome_sign 0.4 3.8
@face nora wren
@face wren nora
@camera between wren nora 7
Wren (neutral): Nora. Ellie's granddaughter. Good, you're here. Wren, mayor. Sorry, I'm already late for something.
Nora (surprised): You know who I am?
Wren (neutral): Everyone does. Your gran told the whole town you'd come home one day. Every Sunday.
Nora (sad): Did she.
Wren (worried): I can't stop, so here's Maple Grove in one breath.
@set act1_arrived
@home barbara off
# the overview points at each building wherever the world editor puts it ("by <building>")
@camera by building_shop 0 3 13 yaw building_shop
Wren (neutral): The Yarn Barn. Rosa sells the wool, and she'll buy whatever you knit.
@camera by building_bakery 0 3 13 yaw building_bakery
Wren (neutral): Heart Bakery. Giorgio. Don't try to pay for your first loaf.
@camera by building_homegoods 0 3 13 yaw building_homegoods
Wren (neutral): Builder's Delight. Steve has tools, seeds and wood. No small talk.
@camera by building_office 0 3 13 yaw building_office
Wren (wry): Willow Homes. That's Gary. Don't worry, he'll find you.
@camera by building_cafe 0 4 20 yaw building_cafe
Wren (neutral): And Sabrina's Cappuccino Cafe. Closes at five. She means it.
@camera between wren nora 7
Wren (neutral): Say hello whenever you like. Your gran's house is down the lane to the west, the one with the roses.
Wren (neutral): Front door sticks: lift it and shove. She left something for you inside.
Nora (warm): Thank you, Wren.
Wren (worried): ...Welcome home, Nora. Really. Sorry. Meeting.
@walk wren 46 4.4 nowait
@wait 1.2
@home wren off
@home giorgio off
@set act1_toured
@goal Go to Gran's house | 7.2 3.0
@camera player


# --- first meetings (Alex, 2026-11-14: after Wren's overview the town is hers to explore; each
# shopkeeper says hello the first time she talks to them). Drafts for Alex.

== meet_rosa
@trigger talk rosa
@requires act1_arrived
@once
@face rosa nora
@camera between rosa nora 6 low
Rosa (happy): Ellie's girl! Oh, you've got her chin. I'm Rosa. Yarn, needles, and I'll buy anything you knit!
Rosa (wry): Your gran was my best customer for thirty years. And my worst payer.
@set met_rosa
@camera player

== meet_giorgio
@trigger talk giorgio
@requires act1_arrived
@once
@face giorgio nora
@camera between giorgio nora 6
Giorgio (warm): New face. Here, this one's on the house. Don't argue, cara, I've already buttered it.
Nora (warm): Thank you. It smells incredible.
Giorgio (warm): Eat. You've come a long way, I can see it. Whatever it was, it's a long way behind you now.
@set met_giorgio
@camera player

== meet_gary
@trigger talk gary
@requires act1_arrived
@once
@face gary nora
@camera between gary nora 6
Gary (wry): Gary, Willow Homes. Property, land, prospects. You must be Ellie's girl, minding Birchfield. Brave.
Gary (happy): Don't worry, everyone starts somewhere. I'll drop by and show you where people end up.
@set met_gary
@camera player

== meet_steve
@trigger talk steve
@requires act1_arrived
@once
@face steve nora
@camera between steve nora 6
Steve (neutral): ...Welcome.
Steve (neutral): Tools. Seeds. Furniture. Hoes are cheap.
Nora (wry): Is that the whole speech?
Steve (neutral): That's two.
@set met_steve
@camera player

== meet_sabrina
@trigger talk sabrina
@requires act1_arrived
@once
@face sabrina nora
@camera between sabrina nora 6
Sabrina (neutral): Hi. Coffee's six coins. We close at five.
Nora (warm): I'm Nora. Ellie's granddaughter.
Sabrina (neutral): I know. Everyone knows. Coffee's still six coins.
@set met_sabrina
@camera player

== act1_note
@trigger area cottage_inside
@requires act1_toured
@once
@goal
@camera 3.6 2.6 9
> Dust on everything. The clock on the mantel stopped at twenty past four.
Nora (sad): Hi, Gran.
> It still smells like her. Lanolin and woodsmoke and the lemon drops she kept in her apron.
@walk nora 4.0 3.9
@face nora 4.0 3.0
@camera 4.0 3.0 4
> On the table, propped against an old biscuit tin, a folded note. Gran's handwriting, all loops and hurry.
Nora (surprised): "For my Nora."
@farm note
> "My darling Nora. By the time you read this I'll be in Florida at your great-aunt Dot's, feet up, complaining about the heat. The doctor says my chest can't take another winter in this valley."
> "So the house is yours to look after while I'm gone. Keep it warm for me. Put a little in the tin each week. Not because the house needs the money. Because a home you pay into is a home you stay in."
> "My needles are in the basket by the rocking chair, with the last three skeins off our own sheep. Make something with your hands. It always helped me. It will help you."
> "Whatever happened out there, love, it stays out there. In here it's just you and the kettle. I'll write: Barbara brings the post at nine. All my love, always. Gran."
Nora (sad): ...Okay. Okay, Gran.
> She folds the note into her pocket. In the basket by the rocking chair: Gran's old needles, worn pale where her fingers held them, and three skeins of cream wool.
@give wool 3
@toast Gran's note is in your bag, with her needles and 3 wool. Rent: 90c a week, into her tin on the table.
@set act1_note
@goal Knit your first sweater in Gran's rocking chair | 2.4 3.6
@toast Click the rocking chair and choose Knit.
@camera player

== act1_knit
@trigger event knit_done
@requires act1_note
@once
@goal
# memory thread #1: the first thing she knits in years brings back the last thing she knit
@camera player 4
@memory on 1.6
> The last stitch closes. She holds the piece up to the window, and her hands remember another sweater.
> Navy, with a cream band across the chest. He'd said cream made him look soft, so she made the band thin.
Max: You made this? Babe. You know I don't really do wool.
> Four months of it. Evenings, mostly, after he'd gone to bed, so it would be a surprise.
Max: Don't make that face. It's sweet. It's just not... me.
> In the morning it was in the bin by the back door, under the coffee grounds. He said it must have fallen in.
> She didn't knit again for six years.
@memory off 1.6
@journal memory The navy sweater | Four months of evenings. A thin cream band, because cream made him look soft. It ended up in the bin under the coffee grounds and I didn't knit again for six years. Today I did.
Nora (sad): ...Okay. That one still stings.
@set act1_knit
> Three quick raps at the door, like someone with somewhere else to be.
@place wren 5.4 3.0 270
@walk wren 3.7 3.3
@face wren nora
@face nora wren
@camera between wren nora 4.5
Wren (neutral): Sorry, the door was open. Ellie left her spare keys at the office and I— oh.
Wren (surprised): Wow. That's beautiful. Did you just make that?
Nora (worried): It's nothing. It's my first one in years, the tension's—
Wren (happy): Nora. I'd wear that to the council meeting. How much is it?
Nora (surprised): How much? I hadn't... thought about it.
Wren (wry): Then think about it now. Name your price, and I'll tell you if you're robbing me.
@set act1_wren_asked
@goal Name your price for Wren
@farm sale wren
@camera player

== act1_sold
@trigger event first_sale
@requires act1_wren_asked
@once
@goal
@face wren nora
@face nora wren
@camera between wren nora 4.5
Wren (happy): Sold. My sister's going to be so jealous.
Wren (neutral): Now, advice from someone who runs a town on no money: don't sit on it. Steve at Builder's Delight sells seed, and Ellie's beds out front are still dug. Grow your own food and every coin goes further.
Wren (wry): And Rosa at the Yarn Barn sells wool. You'll want more of it. A lot more, I think.
Nora (warm): Seeds, then yarn. Thank you, Wren. Really.
@walk wren 7.6 3.0 nowait
@wait 1.2
@home wren off
@set act1_sold
@camera player
@goal Buy turnip seeds from Steve at Builder's Delight | 47.7 -9.4

== act1_seeds
@trigger event seeds_bought
@requires act1_sold
@once
@goal
Nora (warm): Turnips. Gran said they were the one thing nobody could kill.
@set act1_seeds
@goal Plant your turnips in Gran's beds by the house | 12.8 0.2
@toast Click one of Gran's beds and choose Plant turnips.

== act1_planted
@trigger event planted
@requires act1_seeds
@once
@goal
Nora (happy): There. Supper, in a few hours. Now: yarn.
@set act1_planted
@goal Buy more yarn from Rosa at the Yarn Barn | 53.27 -9.6

== act1_yarn
@trigger event yarn_bought
@requires act1_planted
@once
@goal
Nora (warm): Good yarn. Gran would approve. She'd also say I paid too much.
@set act1_yarn
@goal Knit another sweater in Gran's rocking chair | 2.4 3.6

== act1_knit2
@trigger event knit_done
@requires act1_yarn
@once
@goal
Nora (happy): Two. Two sweaters in one day. Wren's wearing the first one around town.
Nora (neutral): Rosa runs a stall at the market. Maybe she'd take this one.
@set act1_knit2
@goal Take your sweater to Rosa at the Maple Grove market | 48.5 -5.6

== act1_strays
@trigger area strays
@requires act1_market
@once
@goal
@home rowan 16.4 -12.2
@walk nora 12.2 -12.4
@face nora 13.5 -14
@camera 13.8 -13.4 8
> Two sheep, grazing past the pond like they own the place. No ear tags. Burrs in their wool.
@face rowan nora
@face nora rowan
@camera between rowan nora 6.5
Rowan (wry): Afternoon. Friends of yours?
Nora (surprised): I was about to ask you the same thing.
Rowan (neutral): Not mine. No marks on them. Strays off the ridge, I'd guess. They come down every autumn, looking for somebody soft.
Nora (wry): And they found me.
Rowan (neutral): Rowan. I keep the flock up on the hill. Ellie and I traded favours. Mostly she fed me and I fixed things.
Nora (neutral): Nora. The granddaughter. The one from the city.
Rowan (warm): I know. She talked about you. A lot, actually.
@walk rowan 14.8 -13.0
@anim rowan Work
@camera between rowan nora 7
@wait 0.6
@shake 0.5
> A dead branch gives under his boot with a crack like a gunshot.
Nora (surprised): Ah!
> Her whole body jerks. Her hands are up before she can stop them.
@anim rowan off
@face rowan nora
@face nora rowan
Rowan (worried): Hey. You alright?
? Rowan watches her, careful, the way you'd watch a skittish ewe.
- I'm fine. It just made me jump. -> fine | familiarity rowan +2; set nora_deflected
- Sorry. Loud noises. Long story. -> honest | trust rowan +3; familiarity rowan +2; set nora_opened
@label fine
Rowan (neutral): Right. Course.
> He doesn't push. He does kick the rest of the branch into the long grass, quietly.
@goto keep
@label honest
Rowan (warm): Nothing to be sorry for. I'll tread quieter.
Nora (warm): Thanks.
@label keep
Rowan (neutral): If you want them, they're yours. Finders keepers, out here. But you'll want a pen first, or they'll wander back the way they came.
Nora (worried): Gran's pen is long gone. I've never built anything in my life.
Rowan (wry): Panels, posts and a gate. Sheep lean on everything, so build it like you mean it. Steve at Builder's Delight sells timber.
? What do you say?
- I'll do it. Today. -> deal | familiarity rowan +3
- Could you help? -> nohelp | trust rowan +1; familiarity rowan +1
@label deal
Rowan (wry): Good. I'll come by and lean on it after. You bring tea.
@goto bye
@label nohelp
Rowan (warm): I'll talk you through it. It's your pen, though. That matters, with sheep.
@label bye
@set met_rowan
> He tips the crook at her like a hat and heads off up the hill, whistling at nothing.
@walk rowan 24 4.4 nowait
@wait 2.5
@home rowan off
@set act1_strays
@camera player
@goal Get wood: buy it from Steve at Builder's Delight, or fell a farm tree with an axe | 47.7 -9.4

== act1_wood
@trigger event wood_bought
@requires act1_strays
@once
@goal
Nora (neutral): Right. A pen. Panels, posts and a gate. How hard can it be.
@set act1_wood
@toast Press F (or Build pen) to lay fence panels: 1 wood each. Craft a gate (G) from 2 wood and set it in the fence.
@goal Build a pen with a gate, near the strays | 13.5 -14

== act1_pen
@trigger event pen_built
@requires act1_wood
@once
@goal
Nora (happy): A pen. An actual pen, with an actual gate. Gran, are you seeing this?
> Now the hard part. The strays are still out by the pond, and they don't look like they're in any hurry.
@toast Walk up behind the sheep and they'll move away from you. Or press Tab and play the dog: they shy from him further off. Steer them in through the gate.
@goal Herd the two strays into your pen

== act1_flock
@trigger event sheep_penned
@requires act1_wood
@once
@goal
@camera player 7
Nora (happy): Both of them. In!
> They're already eating the grass inside the pen as if they'd never been anywhere else.
Nora (warm): Welcome home, you two. That makes three of us.
> Their own wool. No more buying it by the skein.
@time 18.5
@set act1_fence_done
@camera player
@goal Head home. It's getting dark | 9.8 3.0

== act1_market
# scene 5: market day. Someone values her work, out loud, in public.
@trigger area market
@requires act1_knit2
@once
@goal
@place rosa by market_stall 0 -0.95 45
@walk nora by market_stall 0 1.6
@face rosa nora
@face nora rosa
@camera between rosa nora 6 low
Rosa (surprised): Hold on. Hold ON. Is that hand-knit?
Nora (worried): It's nothing. It's a first try, the tension's all over the place—
Rosa (happy): Honey, I've sold factory jumpers for eleven years. I know nothing when I see it, and this isn't it.
> Rosa turns the sweater inside out, the way you'd check a melon.
Rosa (happy): Look at those floats. Look at them! Steve! Come and look at this! Steve!
@if has sweater -> sell
Rosa (warm): You've sold it already? Then bring me the next one, before anybody else sees it.
@goto credit
@label sell
@take sweater 1
@give coins 60
Rosa (warm): Sixty coins, and I want the next one before anybody else sees it.
@toast Sold your first sweater: +60 coins
@label credit
@place steve by market_stall 5.0 3.4
@walk steve by market_stall 1.9 1.6
@face steve nora
@face nora steve
@camera between steve nora 6
Steve (neutral): Hm. Good stitches.
Rosa (wry): From Steve, that's a standing ovation.
@face rosa nora
@face nora rosa
@camera between rosa nora 6 low
? Rosa pulls a bundle of oatmeal yarn out from under the counter.
- I can't take that. Let me pay you. -> pay | familiarity rosa +2
- Thank you. Really. -> thanks | trust rosa +2; familiarity rosa +2
@label pay
Rosa (wry): You can. Later. That's what credit is. Your gran invented it, as far as I'm concerned.
@goto give
@label thanks
Rosa (warm): Pay me when the sweaters sell. They will, love.
@label give
@give wool 5
@set rosa_credit
> Five skeins. More than anyone's handed her in a long time, and it isn't even charity. It's a bet on her.
Nora (warm): Thank you. Really.
@journal note Market day | Rosa shouted across the whole plaza. She gave me wool on credit, like I'm someone worth betting on. Sixty coins for something I made with my own hands.
> Somewhere past the stalls, faint on the wind from the farm road, something says "baa". Then something else says it louder.
Rosa (wry): Hear that? Strays off the ridge, this time of year. Catch yourself a couple and you'll never have to pay me for wool again.
@farm strays
@set act1_market
@camera player
@goal Find where that bleating is coming from | 13.5 -14

== act1_porch
# scene 6: the porch at night. She can open up a little or deflect; both are valid, and it sets
# the tone of her and Rowan's arc.
@trigger area porch
@requires act1_fence_done
@once
@goal
@fade out 0.8
@time 21.5
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@camera 11.2 3.0 6
@fade in 1.2
> Night comes down fast out here. No streetlights. Just stars, and a porch light Gran never got round to fixing.
@phone Voicemail: Max
> One new voicemail. Her thumb hovers over it for a while. Then she plays it.
Voicemail: Nora. It's me. Your mum says you're "taking some time." Okay. Take it.
Voicemail: The house is so quiet. Just... call me back. Please. I miss you.
@phone off
Nora (sad): Please. He never used to say please.
> She sits down by the bottom step. The wood is cold through her jeans.
@place rowan 15.0 4.8 270
@walk rowan 11.3 2.5
> A lantern bobs along the fence line, then stops.
@face rowan nora
@face nora rowan
@camera between rowan nora 6
Rowan (neutral): Checking your fence. It's holding. Mostly out of spite.
Rowan (worried): You okay?
? She could tell him. Some of it. Or none of it.
- Not really. My ex keeps calling. I thought I'd left all that in the city. -> open | trust rowan +3; romance rowan +1; familiarity rowan +2; set nora_opened_porch
- I'm fine. Long day. -> deflect | familiarity rowan +1; set nora_deflected_porch
@label open
Rowan (neutral): Some things follow you. Took me two years to stop setting the table for two.
> He doesn't say anything else, and it's exactly the right amount.
Nora (warm): Thank you. For not saying something wise.
Rowan (wry): I don't know anything wise. Ask the sheep.
@goto lantern
@label deflect
Rowan (neutral): Right. Long days are the worst ones.
> He doesn't push. He never seems to.
@label lantern
> He sets the lantern down by the bottom step.
@prop lantern rowan_lantern 10.6 2.3 0
Rowan (warm): Ellie's porch light's been broken for years. Keep that. I know the way home in the dark.
@walk rowan 24 4.4 nowait
@wait 2.0
@home rosa off
@home steve off
@journal note The porch | Max left a voicemail. He misses me, he says. Rowan left his lantern by the step. I didn't ask him to.
@fade out 1.4
@home rowan off
@set act1_done
@title Act 1: Cast On
@sleep
@time 7.5
@weather clear
@place nora 9.8 3.0 90
@camera 12.4 3.0 9
@fade in 1.6
> Morning. In daylight the cottage looks smaller, and a little less sad. There's a lantern by the step.
@title to be continued
@camera player
@toast Act 1 complete. The farm is in your hands now.
